2026-09-20T09:51:01.3329196Z       "body": "### Discussion\r\n\r\n- Proposed and confirmed in Discussion: https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/discussions/16379\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nIn `fastapi/dependencies/utils.py`, `get_stream_item_type(annotation)` checks if the annotation is a subclass or instance of `AsyncIterator` or `AsyncGenerator`.\r\n\r\nHowever, when a route endpoint uses `Annotated[...]` in its return type annotation (e.g. `Annotated[AsyncIterator[str], ...]` or `Annotated[AsyncGenerator[str, None], ...]`), `get_stream_item_type` failed to inspect the inner stream type because `get_origin(annotation)` returns `Annotated` rather than unwrapping to the inner origin type. As a result, FastAPI fell back to non-streaming response handling.\r\n\r\nThis PR unwraps any outer/nested `Annotated` type layers using `get_args(annotation)[0]` before checking `issubclass(origin, (AsyncIterator, AsyncGenerator))`.\r\n\r\n### Checklist\r\n\r\n- [x] This PR links to a GitHub Discussion for the proposed code change.\r\n- [x] I added tests for the change.\r\n- [x] The new or updated tests fail on the main branch and pass on this PR.\r\n- [x] Coverage stays at 100%.\r\n- [x] The documentation explains the change if needed.\r\n\r\n### AI Disclaimer\r\n\r\n- [x] I acknowledge that I am responsible for this PR and have verified the code, tests, and rationale myself.",
